00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:29,050
But?

253
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:31,980
You like me! Is that it?

254
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,847
Would you drop this already?

255
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,477
The young master was calling you.

256
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:36,697
He wants you to bring...

257
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:37,610
the thing.

258
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,280
Now, please, go away!

259
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,120
Hey, hey, hey!

260
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:45,437
You gotta pick your fiancés better, or
Duffy's just gonna keep killing them!

261
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,817
But you know who Duffy
doesn't want to kill?

262
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:48,730
Me!

263
00:13:48,813 --> 00:13:50,597
And you know who's single one
would make a good husband?

264
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,520
Also me!

265
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,780
Just yanking your chain.

266
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,880
You really need me.

267
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:02,580
I don't mind. Stop that!

268
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:08,640
The Colosseum is packed as usual.

269
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:12,380
Thanks for your hard work, Diamante.

270
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,900
The credit is all yours, Duffy.

271
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:19,200
This country owes everything
to its beloved king.

272
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:21,050
Beloved?

273
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:24,740
They're quite fond of you, too.

274
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:26,370
Stop.

275
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,457
You make it sound like I'm
the hero of the Colosseum.

276
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:30,952
Enough with the modesty.

277
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,357
That's exactly what you are.

278
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,270
No, no.

279
00:14:33,353 --> 00:14:34,357
I'm nothing of the sort.

280
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,270
Fine, then.

281
00:14:35,353 --> 00:14:36,183
You're not.

282
00:14:36,266 --> 00:14:37,096
All right!

283
00:14:37,179 --> 00:14:38,009
I'm a hero!

284
00:14:38,092 --> 00:14:39,220
Guilty as charged! A hero!

285
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,837
Fearless and invincible!

286
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,802
But you didn't hear me say that.

287
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,620
Hey! Hey! Hey!

288
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:49,160
I grabbed the thing you asked for.

289
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,580
Duffy, Duffy!

290
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:53,040
You're too close. Too close?

291
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,400
But what?

292
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,340
But I like it.

293
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:57,500
Now sit.

294
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:04,357
When Straw Hat finds out about this,

295
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:08,297
he'll do anything to get it;
then he'll be mine to control.

296
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:12,297
And his new friend law will
be dragged down with him,

297
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:16,757
diamante—I'm going to entrust this to you.

298
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:20,957
I couldn't possibly; it's
far too important—it's fine,

299
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:23,317
you'll know exactly what to do?

300
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,360
to do Stop.

301
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,897
You're making me sound
like some kind of genius.

302
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:27,810
Yes.

303
00:15:27,893 --> 00:15:31,140
I can only entrust this to
a genius like you. No, no.

304
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,657
I'm nothing of the sort.

305
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:34,240
Fine, then. You're not.

306
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,497
All right, fine.

307
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,520
I'm a genius.

308
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:37,900
Guilty as charged.

309
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:41,519
A genius that will dispose
of that fool's Straw Hat.

310
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,738
But you didn't hear me say it, okay?

311
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,457
Don't worry, genius.

312
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:50,940
He won't be able to resist this one.

313
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:58,220
The source of his late brother's
power, the flame flame fruit.

314
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:01,920
He won't dare let anyone get
their hands on this thing.

315
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:13,340
Looming on the horizon
is their destination.

316
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,160
Those rocks!

317
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:17,880
Look, they're huge!

318
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:22,737
Dress Rosa, here we come!

319
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,600
Hey, won't you keep it down?

320
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:26,507
Dopo Bingo's gonna hear you!

321
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:27,760
Not likely.

322
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:30,600
Worry nuts, we're coming! Catch it all!

323
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:36,480
Known as a land of love and
passion, this is Dressrosa.

324
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,662
Hope you're ready for us, Bingo!

325
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:47,470
Dressrosa!

326
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,700
Let's party!

327
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,457
I told you to keep it down, Luffy!

328
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:52,370
Damn it!

329
00:16:52,453 --> 00:16:53,283
What?

330
00:16:53,366 --> 00:16:55,140
We're deep in enemy
territory, you know? Wow!

331
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,873
I just got the tests in, and guess what?

332
00:16:58,240 --> 00:16:59,540
I'm extra super!

333
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:04,520
As soon as we find that factory,
then I'll let my lasers rip! Boo! Ah!

334
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:06,777
Okay, enough with the yelling, please!

335
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,500
I just had a great idea!

336
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:09,890
Momo!

337
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:11,530
Go!

338
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,640
Get off!

339
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:16,100
I am not going to town!

340
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,700
Also, I cannot fly!

341
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,160
I have to stay here!

342
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,677
What do you mean you can't fly?

343
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,317
I've seen you do it back
in that garbage shoe.

344
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:27,857
Remember, I don't—I have no
clue what you're talking about.

345
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:33,197
I'm not lying; he flew for real,
but he doesn't have wings, surely.

346
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:38,477
I would recall that, and even
if I could fly, I can't now.

347
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:41,320
If I did then then what's

348
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:46,810
your name?

349
00:17:46,893 --> 00:17:50,097
It matters not.

350
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:52,997
The point is, I will never do
such a dreadful thing again.

351
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:53,910
I

352
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:57,837
won't fly; you can't make me.

353
00:17:57,920 --> 00:18:00,077
What is your deal?

354
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:02,057
Afraid of heights or what?

355
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:03,980
what How dare you!

356
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:08,620
I am a brilliant samurai!

357
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:12,001
There is nothing in this
entire world that I fear!

358
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:14,800
Shut and hop!

359
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:16,600
I'm on my fist!

360
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:21,180
Okay, he's only eight years old.

361
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:22,380
What the crap!

362
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,277
I don't care if I say it right!

363
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:28,300
I'm gonna be king of the
pirates all day! Ha! So what?

364
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:33,127
I shall be the shogun of Wano someday
And you'll be in the war beneath my face!

365
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:37,960
And if you're a worm or a eel,
then you're a monkey, you ape!

366
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:40,160
Yes, the wood monkeys are awesome!

367
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,900
Enough, Bobanosuke!

368
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,980
We owe him our lives!

369
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,160
Sir Luffy, please forgive him.

370
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:51,680
He is a samurai, but he is
still young and lacks restraint.

371
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,000
That said,

372
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:57,137
perhaps you could show some restraint in
dealing with children, for all our sakes.

373
00:18:57,220 --> 00:19:01,120
If he's such a little coward,
maybe he shouldn't talk so big.

374
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:07,360
Curse it all!

375
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:08,730
Sorry!

376
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,340
Why is he picking on me?

377
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,140
Get off of her!

378
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,075
What's their problem?

379
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:19,350
Uh-huh.

380
00:19:19,433 --> 00:19:20,600
Like father, like son.

381
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:23,497
You samurai are a bunch
of lechers, aren't you?

382
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,020
Mind your tongue, knave!

383
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:29,300
Hey, Kinemar, let's head to town.

384
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:34,900
How should we pervert, uh, I mean convert
our clothes so we don't stand out?

385
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,500
Oh, a disguise.

386
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:37,722
Yes, of course.

387
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:41,820
In Dressrosa, this fashion is
particularly important for women.

388
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:47,288
Allow me to produce appropriate costumes
so that we may enter the town safely.

389
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,365
I think I'm going to like
this Dressrosa place.

390
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:53,960
Give it a rest.

391
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,710
Hey.

392
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:59,040
Better take this.

393
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,653
It might come in handy.

394
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:04,420
It's a VIVRA card?

395
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,330
Yeah.

396
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:09,019
It'll take you to that place
called Zoe I mentioned.

397
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,608
Zoe is going to be the
next stop on my trip.

398
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:16,452
If anything happens to us on
Dressrosa, go straight there.

399
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:20,200
Just in case, right?

400
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:22,640
We should be fine. Who knows?

401
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,980
What's that paper?

402
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,260
A map one of my crew members made.

403
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,360
Kind of sloppy.

404
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:32,720
So this is where we're at,
the west coast of Dressrosa.

405
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,577
The Flamingo's palace is at the center.

406
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:38,307
We'll be responsible
for handing over Caesar.

407
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,977
We'll pass through Dressrosa until
we get to the northern shore.

408
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:45,017
There we'll cross a long bridge
to the island of Greenbit.

409
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:48,017
Why do we have to cross
Dressrosa to get to an island?

410
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,877
We could just take the ship, right?

411
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,790
Together!

412
00:20:50,873 --> 00:20:52,537
I was told that's not possible.

413
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:53,940
Fine, sounds like fun.

414
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,240
Just get me there safely.

415
00:20:56,840 --> 00:21:00,600
As for the Sunny security
team, be wary of enemy attacks.

416
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:04,540
You may have to be our decoy. Wait, what?

417
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:05,661
Is that a thing?

418
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:08,360
We might engage in combat? What?

419
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:10,857
I thought guarding duty
would be the safest.

420
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:13,077
Well, we are in enemy territory, right?

421
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:16,057
But that's okay, because
we've got Sanji to protect us.

422
00:21:16,140 --> 00:21:17,880
He's not here! Sanji!

423
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:20,669
Luffy's team is gone, too!

424
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,337
They're the key to this whole plan.

425
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:24,477
They better not blow it.

426
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,720
Hey, forget about that for a second.

427
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,480
Who's going to protect us?

428
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:36,717
Those who travel here
may find their hearts

429
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:39,976
enchanted by any number of
the kingdom's many wonders.

430
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:48,620
For example, the fields of
beautiful, fragrant flowers.

431
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:55,460
Or perhaps the enticing
aroma of local cuisine.

432
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:01,320
Smells good!

433
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:11,360
After dinner, beautiful women and
passionate dancers may catch your eye.

434
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,380
Looks good!

435
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:20,280
And most remarkable of all...

436
00:22:22,060 --> 00:22:24,500
Hey! Wait! Give it back!

437
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:27,800
Mario! Bad Dog! Bad Dog!

438
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,840
Give me back my arm!

439
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,680
It's not a toy! I need that!

440
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,357
What if the stuffing comes out, huh?

441
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,377
Then what am I gonna do?

442
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:35,872
Give me a break already!

443
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,820
All this money's giving me a side stitch!

444
00:22:40,980 --> 00:22:41,921
And my stuffing!

445
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:43,797
Are they toys?

446
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:46,777
There is a strange sight that awestruck

447
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,625
visitors cannot see
anywhere else in the world.

448
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:51,320
Why, hello there.

449
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:55,760
Just a friendly neighborhood
soldier. Don't mind me.

450
00:22:56,020 --> 00:22:57,020
Hmm, that's odd.

451
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:58,677
Have we met somewhere before?

452
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:00,080
I know your face.

453
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,520
Oh, that's it.

454
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:04,111
You are in today's paper.

455
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:05,540
Oh, no.

456
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:07,497
My strings got all tangled up.

457
00:23:07,580 --> 00:23:08,410
Someone help me.

458
00:23:08,493 --> 00:23:09,800
A toy or a dude?

459
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,840
Hey, Luffy, look at that.

460
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:18,717
Everywhere you look.

461
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:21,637
As if it were nothing peculiar at all.

462
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,917
There are toys.

463
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,860
Living alongside humans.

464
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:32,060
Only outsiders seem perplexed
by these colorful citizens.

465
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:38,857
Love, passion and toys.

466
00:23:38,940 --> 00:23:43,300
Dance together in the streets
here in the port town.

467
00:23:45,820 --> 00:23:48,280
Oh, man's been stabbed in the streets!

468
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:51,140
Oh, not again.

469
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:52,600
Did he say again?

470
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:54,677
You got some maniac on the loose?

471
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:55,590
Is that it?

472
00:23:55,673 --> 00:23:57,480
No, just very passionate women.

473
00:23:57,720 --> 00:24:00,220
And they're the jealous type, you know.

474
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:03,186
So if their lover cheats
on them, for example,

475
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:06,100
things get a little violent. A little?

476
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:09,342
Seems like the pretty ones
are especially stabby.

477
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,937
Okay, the toys are alive.

478
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:16,300
I'm over it now come on let's eat

479
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:27,660
Sir Luffy we cannot afford to whittle away
the hours in this place time is short.

480
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:30,040
I'm a citricongenal promptly

481
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:32,860
Whoa, whoa relax, bro.

482
00:24:33,140 --> 00:24:34,728
I know we gotta move quick.

483
00:24:34,960 --> 00:24:36,901
We can't go running around blind.

484
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:38,620
We gotta gather info first

485
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,997
Hey, isn't this fishy to you?

486
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:46,737
The king of the country abdicated
his throne this morning.

487
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:50,797
I kind of figured this place would be
in chaos, but nobody seems to care.

488
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:53,077
Maybe they haven't heard the news yet?

489
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:55,280
What no way!

490
00:24:57,440 --> 00:25:00,477
Let's ask him, hey pups—stop it!

491
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:01,797
Why is that bad?

492
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:04,277
Because you were on the front
page of the newspaper today!

493
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:05,190
today

494
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:09,037
Thanks for waiting!

495
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:10,620
Your order has arrived!

496
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:12,580
Or has it?

497
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:16,160
Oh, yeah, I think it has! Let's eat!

498
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:18,057
Thresh shrimp Paulie...

499
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:21,017
Roast squid ink pasta...

500
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,760
And fairy pumpkin gazpacho!

501
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:26,837
Looks awesome!

502
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:29,020
It's time to dig in!

503
00:25:31,140 --> 00:25:32,380
So good!

504
00:25:33,260 --> 00:25:35,260
What the heck is a fairy pumpkin?

505
00:25:36,020 --> 00:25:37,780
Well, uh, you see,

506
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:42,520
in this country, many people still
believe in old legends about fairies.

507
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,340
Or do they?

508
00:25:44,660 --> 00:25:45,836
What kind of legend?

509
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:50,460
More like people see fairies. Or do they?

510
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,580
On the island?

511
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:52,930
Indeed.

512
00:25:53,013 --> 00:25:54,040
All the time.

513
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:55,897
Fascinating, right?

514
00:25:55,980 --> 00:25:57,921
It's been that way for centuries.

515
00:25:58,060 --> 00:26:01,717
Although most of us have never
seen them, we all know they exist.

516
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,977
And do you know what people call them?

517
00:26:04,060 --> 00:26:04,900
I'll tell you.

518
